    ("Lygia Clark: Bichos (Creatures)", "Lygia Clark", 1960, "Hinged aluminum panels", "Neo-Concretism / Brazilian", ["kinetic","sculpture","participatory","hinged","interactive"], ["aluminum panels","hinged","creature","interactive","movement"], ["silver aluminum","geometric hinged"], "Various museums", "Hinged aluminum panels that can be folded and unfolded by the viewer into unlimited configurations — a 'living organism' of metal.", "Clark's Bichos (Creatures) require viewer participation to exist. They launch Brazilian Neo-Concretism and participatory art simultaneously.", "female", "Brazilian"),
